# Top-level cmd/gc tests whose failures under GC_TEST_SPLIT_STRICT=1 are known
# flakes, not gate findings: test, tab, the bead that owns the flake, tab, the
# reason. A listed test's failure is reported (KNOWN FLAKY) but does not fail
# the TESTS verdict, and scripts/split-strict-baseline never bakes it into the
# known failures. Flake policy: Bazel retries are pinned off repo-wide
# (scripts/bazel_no_flaky_retries_test.go), so the lane does not retry; a test
# that flakes is listed here with an owner bead, and leaves when the bead
# closes.
TestExternalReadsResumeServesNoPreSuspensionScaleCheck	mc-19h7i	straddle=true subtest times out under remote load ("before suspending: ok not trusted"); passes locally under the gate
TestManagedDoltSIGKILLLockGateRefusesWhenAnotherDatabaseIsHeld	mc-ncbsc	the lock gate reads /proc/locks after the flock probe; under host load the holder is gone by then ("flock probe reports held but lock-holder inspection found no holder"), so the refusal names the wrong pid. Unrelated to the split.
